                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 58.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 251.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 11, 1870</date>. (Received August
                    23.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you herewith a
                    copy of a letter I addressed to the Duke de Gramont, together with the
                    translation of his reply. The correspondence explains itself.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>



